== 4.9 Chapter 4 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The products of photosynthesis are],
  [starch and carbon dioxide],
  [carbon dioxide and water],
  [glucose and oxygen],
  [oxygen and water]
)

#mcq(2, [The layer of the leaf that contains most chloroplasts is the],
  [upper epidermis],
  [lower epidermis],
  [palisade mesophyll],
  [spongy mesophyll]
)

#mcq(3, [In the starch test, the leaf is boiled in ethanol in order to],
  [soften the leaf],
  [kill the cells],
  [dissolve the starch],
  [remove the chlorophyll]
)

#mcq(4, [If the rate of photosynthesis stops rising as light intensity increases, the limiting factor could be],
  [water],
  [chlorophyll],
  [leaf area],
  [carbon dioxide concentration]
)

#mcq(5, [Photosynthesis takes place in the],
  [nucleus],
  [ribosomes],
  [chloroplasts],
  [mitochondria]
)

#mcq(6, [The gas released during photosynthesis is],
  [hydrogen],
  [oxygen],
  [nitrogen],
  [carbon dioxide]
)

#mcq(7, [A variegated leaf is used in experiments on photosynthesis because],
  [it has no stomata],
  [only its green parts contain chlorophyll],
  [it respires faster],
  [it is larger]
)

#mcq(8, [The main function of the waxy cuticle is to],
  [absorb light],
  [store starch],
  [allow gas exchange],
  [reduce water loss]
)

#mcq(9, [Chlorophyll appears green because it],
  [converts light to green],
  [produces green light],
  [reflects green light],
  [absorbs green light]
)

#mcq(10, [The raw materials for photosynthesis are],
  [carbon dioxide and water],
  [glucose and oxygen],
  [starch and water],
  [oxygen and water]
)

#mcq(11, [Glucose made in a leaf may be stored as],
  [starch],
  [protein in the chloroplast],
  [glycogen],
  [cellulose in the vacuole]
)

#mcq(12, [Which of the following would reduce the rate of photosynthesis?],
  [Increasing light intensity],
  [Closing the stomata],
  [Raising the temperature to 25 °C],
  [Raising the carbon dioxide concentration]
)

#mcq(13, [The air spaces in the spongy mesophyll are important because they],
  [contain chlorophyll],
  [allow gases to diffuse to and from the cells],
  [store water],
  [carry sugar]
)

#mcq(14, [The upper epidermis is transparent because],
  [it is covered with wax],
  [it contains no chloroplasts and lets light through],
  [it stores starch],
  [it has many stomata]
)

#mcq(15, [Photosynthesis converts],
  [light energy to chemical energy],
  [heat energy to light energy],
  [chemical energy to light energy],
  [chemical energy to heat energy]
)

#mcq(16, [The element that is a component of chlorophyll is],
  [calcium],
  [magnesium],
  [potassium],
  [iron]
)

#mcq(17, [A plant kept in the dark for 48 hours is said to be],
  [turgid],
  [wilting],
  [etiolated],
  [destarched]
)

#mcq(18, [Which factor would most likely be limiting for a plant in a sealed glass jar in bright light?],
  [Light intensity],
  [Leaf area],
  [Chlorophyll content],
  [Carbon dioxide concentration]
)

#mcq(19, [Water enters the leaf through the],
  [cuticle],
  [xylem],
  [stomata],
  [phloem]
)

#mcq(20, [The starch test on a leaf uses],
  [Biuret reagent],
  [Benedict's solution],
  [ethanol alone],
  [iodine solution]
)

#mcq(21, [Which of these is *not* a fate of glucose in a plant?],
  [Conversion to cellulose for cell walls],
  [Conversion to haemoglobin for transport],
  [Conversion to sucrose for transport],
  [Conversion to starch for storage]
)

#mcq(22, [Photosynthesis in a plant stops at night because],
  [there is no light to drive the light-dependent reaction],
  [the plant respires only at night],
  [the chlorophyll is destroyed],
  [the stomata close permanently]
)

#mcq(23, [The compensation point is reached when],
  [respiration stops],
  [the rate of photosynthesis equals the rate of respiration],
  [the plant wilts],
  [photosynthesis stops]
)

#mcq(24, [Which of the following is an advantage of the leaf being thin?],
  [It contains more chlorophyll],
  [It can store more starch],
  [Gases reach the cells over a short distance],
  [It loses less water]
)

#mcq(25, [The veins of a leaf contain],
  [only xylem],
  [only phloem],
  [both xylem and phloem],
  [neither xylem nor phloem]
)

#mcq(26, [A plant deficient in nitrogen would be expected to],
  [grow taller than normal],
  [have purple leaves],
  [grow poorly with yellow leaves],
  [produce more chlorophyll]
